  "id": "brachmannde-lange-syndrome",
  "term": "Brachmann–de Lange syndrome",
  "definition": "Brachmann–de Lange syndrome is a biological syndrome involving slowed growth and short stature, severe intellectual disability, distinctive head and facial features, excess body hair, a low-pitched growling cry, and hand malformations. It can appear sporadically or be linked to autosomal dominant inheritance or duplication of the long arm of chromosome 3.",
